Serve Config
===============================================================================

The `serve` section configures `mech serve` and browser-oriented project serving.

```mech
config := {
  serve: {
    address: "127.0.0.1"
    port: 8081
    paths: ["demo.mec"]
    shim: "index.html"
    wasm: "../../src/wasm/pkg"
    stylesheets: ["style.css"]
  }
}
```

1. Fields
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

| Field | Description |
|-------|-------------|
| `address` | Server bind address. Defaults to `127.0.0.1`. |
| `port` | Server port. Defaults to `8081`. |
| `paths` | Source files or recursive source directories composed with `run.paths`. |
| `shim` | HTML shim that explicitly owns the served root page. |
| `wasm` | Path to a wasm package directory. |
| `stylesheets` | Stylesheets to include with formatted output. |

2. Workspace composition
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Configured serving uses the same runtime workspace as `mech serve file.mec` and
`mech serve directory`. `run.paths` are selected first, followed by additional
`serve.paths`; duplicates retain their first position. File entries become
explicit targets and directory entries are discovered recursively.

Browser-project routes compose with the source-document routes:

| Route | Response |
|-------|----------|
| `/foo.mec` | Formatted Mech HTML. |
| `/foo.html` | Formatted Mech HTML alias. |
| `/foo` | Extensionless formatted Mech HTML alias. |
| `/source/foo.mec` | Raw Mech source. |
| `/code/foo.mec` | Encoded syntax tree. |
| `/mech.mcfg` | The loaded project configuration. |
| `/_mech/project-sources.json` | Current source inventory using `/source/...` URLs. |

The project JS and WASM package routes remain under `/_mech/`. Workspace watch
refresh updates both formatted sources and the project source inventory.

3. Project root
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

A configured browser application that must own `/` supplies a real
`index.html` or configures `serve.shim`. Otherwise the server chooses the first
selected source, `index.mec`, a single source, or a generated source listing.
Configured browser assets do not hide source-document routes.

4. Browser host config injection
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

When browser host settings or run grants are configured, `mech serve` derives a browser host config projection and injects it into the served shim.

Browser pages can initialize from that projection with `WasmMech.fromHostConfig()`.

5. Static bundling
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

`bundle-web` requires nonempty `run.paths` and `serve.paths` from the project config. It reads the `serve` section to determine project sources and stylesheets; the shim and wasm package may come from the config or the `--shim` and `--wasm` command-line options. Static bundles require relative browser URLs; server-root URLs such as `/_mech/project.js` are not portable in static output.
